<div class="qul-docs">
  <h2>About surah information</h2>

  <p>
    This resource holds background reading for each surah: its main themes and topics, the circumstances
    of its revelation, a summary, and other context that helps a reader place the surah.
  </p>

  <p>
    It is available in several languages, as <strong>SQLite</strong>, <strong>CSV</strong> and
    <strong>JSON</strong>. Some languages ship two versions — a short summary and a longer article.
  </p>

  <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-info">
    The long version contains HTML tags for headings, paragraphs and emphasis, so render it as HTML
    rather than as plain text.
  </div>

  <h2>Data format</h2>
  <p>
    The JSON file is one object keyed by surah number. The CSV file and the <code>surah_infos</code> table of the
    SQLite file have the same fields, one row per surah.
  </p>
  <div class="docs-code">
    <div class="docs-code-header"><span>JSON</span></div>
    <pre><code>{
  "1": {
    "surah_number": 1,
    "surah_name": "Al-Fatihah",
    "text": "&lt;h2&gt;Name&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Surah is named Al-Fatihah because of its subject matter...&lt;/p&gt;",
    "short_text": "This Surah is named Al-Fatihah because of its subject matter..."
  }
}</code></pre>
  </div>
  <ul>
    <li><code>surah_number</code>: the surah, 1 to 114.</li>
    <li><code>surah_name</code>: the surah's transliterated name, such as <code>Al-Fatihah</code>, in every language.</li>
    <li><code>text</code>: the long article, as HTML.</li>
    <li><code>short_text</code>: a short summary. Empty for some languages.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
    
